Language choice seems to be a very personal thing, and could easily 
become a Holy War.

However, I suspect that the most portable GUI language is Java. I 
further suspect that a JRE is far more likely to be present on a machine 
than either Python or the .NET runtime. Java is also object oriented, 
does garbage collection and hides pointers. Python may be easier to code 
- I keep meaning to learn it properly.

I personally would only use C or C++ for a new project when either speed 
(e.g. realtime app) or low-level control (e.g. a virtual machine) is 
vital.

